
`native/` holds the AUnit tests for InterfaceSprayer/ImplementSprayer/ConfigSprayer/RemoteSprayer/RemoteLineBuffer
(../lib/LoofdoesCore/src/), run natively (no ESP32 attached). The shared
guidance library they build against (../../MeijWorks Libs/VehicleGuidance)
has its own suite in Ploegbesturing Isobus' native build:

- `native/tests/` -- one `test_<ClassName>.cpp` per class under test.
- `native/support/` -- a small, self-contained set of Arduino-shaped stubs
  (Print/Stream/Arduino.h/etc.), not a real EpoxyDuino dependency, plus
  `native_main.cpp` (the host `int main()` entry point). These stand in only
  for the Arduino framework: the guidance data model and receiver port
  (`GuidanceSource`, `SerialGuidanceChannel` from `MeijWorks Libs/
  VehicleGuidance`) are the real classes, fed through a fake `HardwareSerial`
  in `test_RemoteSprayer.cpp`. No native stub exists for them.
- `native/LoofdoesNativeTests.cpp` -- the single AUnit driver (`setup()`/
  `loop()`), matching Salacia's `test/native/SalaciaNativeTests.cpp` pattern.
  Every `test_*.cpp` file only registers `test(...)` blocks; none of them
  define `setup()`/`loop()` themselves anymore, so they all link into one
  combined binary instead of one binary per test file.
- `native/run_tests_msvc.ps1` -- MSVC fallback for Windows without GCC.

```
pio run -e native
.pio/build/native/program(.exe)
```

Needs a real host C++17 compiler on PATH (g++ or clang++) -- on Windows
without one, use test\native\run_tests_msvc.ps1 instead, which builds and
runs the same combined binary via MSVC directly. That script passes
`/Zc:preprocessor` -- MSVC's legacy preprocessor mishandles AUnit's
`test(SuiteName, testName)` argument-count dispatch, which every test in
this project uses (matching Salacia's convention: groups each test's display
name under the class it exercises, e.g. `InterfaceSprayer_button1_...`,
`ImplementSprayer_doseLHA_...`).

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing (not used here -- pio test's
own Unity-based runner doesn't understand this project's AUnit setup):
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
